From 90d349cca896f27780cf5ce10b2102ebe372b930 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:59:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] perf(modules): provider command facts follow CDB generations

Fresh project-module facades rebuilt the complete producer and consumer index even when their compilation database and adjusted commands were unchanged. Retain one lazy first-command inventory per directory CDB generation and reuse the immutable provider index only after exact adjusted-command equality. Per-file configuration still runs on each fresh facade; raw response-file commands bypass memoization and source provider hints still require a fresh dependency scan. Focused regressions cover generation replacement with live old facades, mangler changes and reversion, independent response-file changes, and renamed module sources.
